# 2026-10-01 — Renamed Owner account aoadmin -> admin (operator-approved)

README §19.3 / ST-13. Operator instruction: "make the account admin instead of
aoadmin and link them." Approved with alias (alsoKnownAs) to preserve old links.

## Why `aoadmin` existed — and why the README was WRONG about why

README claimed "`admin` is a reserved username in Mastodon". That is **not
hardcoded**. It comes from a per-instance **setting**:

    /opt/mastodon/app/validators/unreserved_username_validator.rb
      settings_reserves_username? -> Setting.reserved_usernames.include?(username)

    $ rails runner
    reserved_usernames=["admin","support","help","root","webmaster",
                        "administrator","mod","moderator"]
    includes 'admin' => true
    Devise.pam_authentication=false        # so the PAM path is irrelevant here

The name was freeable by editing the setting. No code change, no image change.

## Change applied

    1. Setting.reserved_usernames -= ["admin"]
       ["admin","support",...] -> ["support","help","root","webmaster",
                                   "administrator","mod","moderator"]
    2. Account.update!(username: 'admin', also_known_as: [old_aoadmin_uri])
       inside ActiveRecord::Base.transaction
    3. uri/url updated separately (see trap below)

Account id 117363090403638110 throughout - no new account created.

## Verified live

    id: https://mastodon.300x3.com/users/admin
    preferredUsername: admin
    alsoKnownAs: ['https://mastodon.300x3.com/users/aoadmin']
    inbox: https://mastodon.300x3.com/users/admin/inbox
    webfinger acct:admin@mastodon.300x3.com -> 200
    webfinger acct:aoadmin@mastodon.300x3.com -> 404   (expected; alias is at actor level)

Integrity: email still admin@300x3.com; followers preserved (bot still follows);
0 accounts left pointing at the old aoadmin uri; exactly 1 local account named
admin. mastodon-web/streaming/db/redis/sidekiq and the OpenClaw bridge all
unchanged and active.

## Why this also fixes the ghost profile

Earlier finding: mastodon.social held a stale cached `admin@mastodon.300x3.com`
(account id 117327389970897359) that did not exist in our DB, so a follow
directed at it was delivered to an inbox with no local match and vanished. The
real account now occupies `.../users/admin` again, so that handle resolves. The
follow still has to be re-sent by the operator.

## Traps

- **`Account#update!(username:)` does NOT rewrite `uri`/`url`.** After the rename
  the row read `username=admin` but `uri=.../users/aoadmin` — a split identity.
  ActivityPub follows `uri`, not `username`, so federation would still have used
  the old actor. Fixed with an explicit
  `Account.where(id:).update_all(uri:, url:)`. **Always check `uri` after a rename.**
